uce` seed rather than adding it separately after the loop.\n- **Fewest Elements (Rule 4) / APP**: Eliminated the mutable `let premium` accumulator and `for` loop in favor of `reduce`, removing all assignment mutations (mass −12) and lowering total mass from ~45 to ~36.\n\n**Rule 1**: All tests remained green throughout.\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\nRefactoring: Extracted itemPremium/quotePremium helpers, named the surcharge\n             constant, replaced mutating loop with declarative reduce.\nMass Change: ~45 -> ~36 (delta -9)\nTests: All passing (2 passed | 41 todo)\n```\n\nNote for the next Red phase: the current `itemPremium` applies the 10% surcharge per-item, but the spec (see `it.todo(\"first insurance carries 10% initial assessment surcharge\")` and the multi-item example `cursed sword + plain amulet -> 210 G before ... fee`) suggests the 10% is a *policy-wide* first-insurance surcharge, not per-item. This will likely need restructuring once those tests are activated — kept as-is now since it satisfies all currently-passing tests."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-48-37_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 2\nRecent Green phase: Added BASE_PREMIUM table for sword/amulet/staff/potion; quote sums each item base + 10% first insurance surcharge + processing fee.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 2\nRecent Green phase: Added BASE_PREMIUM table for sword/amulet/staff/potion; q