n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784908596828},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Red Phase Complete:\n**Test Activated**: \"cursed sword adds 50% of item base premium\"\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: impl ignores cursed → 115, not 165 Correct\n\n## Green -- add curse surcharge (50% of item base) for main items\n\nThe curse surcharge is item-specific. I need item-level modifiers. The first-insurance is applied to base only. Let me restructure: accumulate base premium and item-specific surcharges separately. Curse adds 50% of item base to the item surcharge pool."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012utWwPFuBDFHYCWtrjitgt","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst isComponent = (type: string): boolean => !(type in BASE_PREMIUM);\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (type: string): number => BASE_PREMIUM[type];\n\nconst itemSurcharge = (item: Item, base: number): number =>\n  item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n\nconst componentGroupBasePremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const componentCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  let surcharges = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(item.type, (componentCounts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      const base = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n      basePremium += base;\n      surcharges += itemSurcharge(item, base);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of componentCounts.values()) {\n    basePremium += componentGroupBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  return PROCESSING_FEE + basePremium + surcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge;\n};","oldText":"co