 is clearer at the call site. Per the priority premise, **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps raw APP mass**.\n\n## Step 6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Naming (Rule 2)**: Extracted `isLoyalCustomer(customer)` predicate to name the domain concept previously buried in the inline `customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD` comparison.\n- The loyalty-discount expression now reads as domain logic: `isLoyalCustomer(customer) ? base * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0`.\n\nBenefits:\n- Loyalty eligibility is now a single, self-documenting concept, reusable when future tests (the pending \"second contract\" / integration cases) also need the loyalty condition.\n- Aligns the loyalty check with the existing `SURCHARGE_RULES` predicate style (`applies:` functions), improving consistency.\n\nRules 3 (No Duplication) and 4 (Fewest Elements): No other duplication or unnecessary abstraction found; the surcharge-rule table and component-grouping helpers are already minimal and single-sourced.\n\n## Step 7: Report\n\n**Refactoring Complete**\n- **Refactoring**: Extracted `isLoyalCustomer` predicate to reveal domain intent (Rule 2).\n- **Mass Change**: ~28 → ~28 (neutral; clarity gain, and Rule 2 trumps APP).\n- **Tests**: All 19 passing, 24 todo."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-48-37_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added policy-wide loyalty discount (20% of policy base premium when customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= 2). quotePremium now takes the customer and subtracts the loyalty discount.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","cont