8519},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tests still pass.\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass (`quotePremium`)\n\n```\nconst quotePremium = (items, context): number => {\n  const { base, surcharges } = sumItemPremiums(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = base * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  return PROCESSING_FEE + base + surcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge - totalDiscount(base, context);\n};\n```\n\n- Bindings: items, context, base, surcharges, firstInsuranceSurcharge + refs ≈ 11 → 11\n- Invocations: sumItemPremiums, totalDiscount, arithmetic (`*`×1, `+`×3, `-`×1) ≈ 7 → 14\n- Conditionals: 0 → 0\n- Constants: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass ≈ 25** (vs. ~50 before, for the `quotePremium` function body).\n\nNote: mass moved into `DISCOUNT_RULES` + `totalDiscount`, but that mirrors the existing `SURCHARGE_RULES` pattern, so the *conceptual* footprint shrinks even though a small reusable helper was added. The two ad-hoc conditionals are gone.\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: The two discount computations used the same ad-hoc pattern (`condition ? base * rate : 0`) — conceptual duplication and inconsistent with the existing `SURCHARGE_RULES` table. Extracted a parallel `DISCOUNT_RULES` table + `totalDiscount` helper, mirroring the additive-surcharge design.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Introduced a `QuoteContext` type bundling `customer` + `isFollowUp`, so `quotePremium` now takes a single meaningful context object instead of three positional args. Adding future discount rules (e.g. bundle discounts) is now a one-line table entry.\n- **Naming**: All names kept — they accurately describe purpose. New names (`DISCOUNT_RULES`, `totalDiscount`, `QuoteContext`) follow the established vocabulary.\n- **APP Mass**: `quotePremium` body reduced ~50 → ~25, eliminating 2 conditionals.\n\nBenefits: symmetric, table-driven treatment of surcharges *and* discounts; fewer conditionals; easier extension.\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n**Refactoring Complete:**\n- **Refactoring**: Extracted `DISCOUNT_RULES` table + `totalDiscount` helper (mirroring `SURCHARGE_RULES`); introduced `QuoteContext` to replace positional args in `quotePremium`.\n- **Mass Change**: `quotePremium` body ~50 → ~25 (removed 2 conditionals).\n- **Tests**: All 21 passing (22 todo remain)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1486,"output":1018,"cacheRead":18331,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":20835,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784908978519,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ec872e08-8a71-4b28-9f18-44459698a758","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":18922,"output":5147,"cacheRead":64508,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":20835,"turns":5},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784908991483},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me check the current state to stay in sync with refactored code."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Nc9eSqvLjZRB9Pduo6HDVQ","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":95,"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-48-37_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1881,"output":164,"cacheRead":68000,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":70045,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784908991486,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-602480a5-4b8e-428f-b4fc-7bd9dd91d453","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Nc9eSqvLjZRB9Pduo6HDVQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"}\n\nconst sumItemPremiums = (items: Item[]): ItemPremiums => {\n  const componentCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  let base = 0;\n  let surcharges = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(item.type, (componentCounts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      const itemBase = basePremiumFor(item.type);\n      base += itemBase;\n      surcharges += itemSurcharge(item, itemBase);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const count of componentCounts.values()) {\n    base += componentGroupBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  return { base, surcharges };\n};\n\nconst isLoyalCustomer = (customer: Customer): boolean =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n\ninterface QuoteContext {\n  customer: Customer;\n  isFollowUp: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface DiscountRule {\n  applies: (context: QuoteContext) => boolean;\n  rate: number;\n}\n\nconst DISCOUNT_RULES: DiscountRule[] = [\n  { applies: (context) => isLoyalCustomer(context.customer), rate: LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE },\n  { applies: (context) => context.isFollowUp, rate: FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE },\n];\n\nconst totalDiscount = (base: number, context: QuoteContext): number =>\n  DISCOUNT_RULES.filter((rule) => rule.applies(context)).reduce(\n    (total, rule) => total + base * rule.rate,\n    0\n  );\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[], context: QuoteContext): number => {\n  const { base, surcharges } = sumItemPremiums(items);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = base * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  return PROCESSING_FEE + base + surcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge - totalDiscount(base, context);\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n      quoteCount += 1;\n      return { premium: quotePremium(step.items, { customer: scenario.customer, isFollowUp }) };\n    }\n    return { premium: PROCESSING_FEE };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isE